A||||6||DecadenceR||E-Brake||||5||
Z||000000||DecadenceR||07-11-2001||09:34 PM||||My e-brake doesn't work. I can take the cables out of the 86 before it goes, but I don't know what to do because I have never removed an e-brake. Any tips or suggestions or easy ways to do it?<BR>I know I have to replace the cables on the driver side. The passenger side works if you pull the cable itself underneath, but the e-brake doesn't do up when you pull it.||||reg||5
Z||000001||DecadenceR||07-12-2001||12:29 AM||||*bump*||||reg||1
Z||000002||Indiana_resto_guy||07-12-2001||12:36 AM||||Remove the adjuster from the system by totally unscrewing the rod from the nut. <BR>this will isolate the drivers side cable, give it a tug and see if it moves. Then try the e-brake handle and see what you have. Since you already stated that the passenger side moves with a tug, it leaves only those 2.||||reg||1
Z||000003||theogre||07-12-2001||08:04 PM||||Indy, good idea. If you can get the bloody nut off w/o wrecking something.... you know how that one goes...<P>Dec,<BR>Jack and jackstand the car.<P>Take the wheel off, then you can easily see if the thing is moving.<P>If it doesn't move try grabbing the level on the back of the caliper with big pliers and see if that moves. If that moves and the cable didn't,,, well,,, <P>If the inside handle won't move then the stupid main cable is probably cooked inside.<P>To get at the main handle you have to remove the plastic trim and boot. the reast is pretty stright forward.<p>[This message has been edited by theogre (edited 07-12-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000004||DecadenceR||07-12-2001||09:48 PM||||Well I started the quest today... Turns out it was the main cable, AND the driver side cable. Ordered them both from the Fiero Store today, so I'll probably have them monday. It was a pain to remove the cables, but a LOT easier than I had expected. I thought I was gonna have another 6 hour job ahead of me... LOL||||reg||1
Z||000005||theogre||07-12-2001||11:31 PM||||When you put them on make sure they can't touch the exhaust. That's probably why those 2 are shot.<P>Check clearance with them free and with the handle tight. They move.<P>There's suposed to be an S shaped wire that holds the main one off the exhaust. Use what ever you have to to make sure they don't cook but don't bind the main jacket either The cable jacket must move to work right.||||reg||1
Z||000006||DecadenceR||07-13-2001||02:11 AM||||The s-shaped hooks are still there. It does look like these were damaged though.. The one cable looks like it started to open itself up. Like you san see the plastic coating startred to stretch itself apart. And the other cable was missing the outer protection for about 5 incheas near where it goes to the brake itself. I'd have to show you pics, it's hard to actually describe.||||reg||1
